    "diff_hunk": "@@ -42071,11 +42071,16 @@ interface <dfn>HTMLLabelElement</dfn> : <span>HTMLElement</span> {\n \n   <div w-nodev>\n \n-  <p><span data-x=\"category-label\">Labelable elements</span> have a <code>NodeList</code> object\n-  associated with them that represents the list of <code>label</code> elements, in <span>tree\n-  order</span>, whose <span>labeled control</span> is the element in question. The <dfn><code data-x=\"dom-lfe-labels\">labels</code></dfn> IDL attribute of <span\n-  data-x=\"category-label\">labelable elements</span>, on getting, must return that\n-  <code>NodeList</code> object.</p>\n+  <p><span data-x=\"category-label\">Labelable elements</span> and all <code>input</code> elements\n+  have a <code>NodeList</code> object associated with them that represents the list of\n+  <code>label</code> elements, in <span>tree order</span>, whose <span>labeled control</span> is the\n+  element in question. The <dfn><code data-x=\"dom-lfe-labels\">labels</code></dfn> IDL attribute of\n+  <span data-x=\"category-label\">labelable elements</span> and <code>input</code> elements, on\n+  getting, must return that <code>NodeList</code> object, and that same value must always be\n+  returned, unless this element is an <code>input</code> element whose <code\n+  data-x=\"attr-input-type\">type</code> attribute is in the <span\n+  data-x=\"attr-input-type-hidden\">Hidden</span> state, in which case it must instead return\n+  null.</p>",
